{# ------------------------------------------------ QUESTIONS: INSTRUMENT #}
<section class="diagnostic chapter" id="questions" data-chapter="04" data-title="Questions" data-q="0">
  <div class="diag-grid">
    <div class="diag-copy">
      <p class="kicker"><span class="node-dot node-dot-ochre"></span>How Communitygeeks thinks</p>
      <h2 class="diag-h2">What are people trying to do, and what happens next?</h2>
      <p class="diag-intro">Every engagement starts from the same set of questions, before any recommendation gets made.</p>
      <ol class="qlist" role="group" aria-label="Diagnostic questions">
        <li><button class="qnode" type="button" data-q="0" aria-pressed="true"><span class="qnode-dot"></span><span class="qnode-idx">01</span><span class="qnode-text">Who participates around your product?</span></button></li>
        <li><button class="qnode" type="button" data-q="1" aria-pressed="false"><span class="qnode-dot"></span><span class="qnode-idx">02</span><span class="qnode-text">What makes participation worthwhile?</span></button></li>
        <li><button class="qnode" type="button" data-q="2" aria-pressed="false"><span class="qnode-dot"></span><span class="qnode-idx">03</span><span class="qnode-text">Where do those groups actually interact?</span></button></li>
        <li><button class="qnode" type="button" data-q="3" aria-pressed="false"><span class="qnode-dot"></span><span class="qnode-idx">04</span><span class="qnode-text">Who acts on what participants reveal?</span></button></li>
        <li><button class="qnode" type="button" data-q="4" aria-pressed="false"><span class="qnode-dot"></span><span class="qnode-idx">05</span><span class="qnode-text">What happens after someone contributes?</span></button></li>
        <li><button class="qnode" type="button" data-q="5" aria-pressed="false"><span class="qnode-dot"></span><span class="qnode-idx">06</span><span class="qnode-text">Where does participation break down?</span></button></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="diag-instrument">
      <div class="diag-instrument-head"><span>Participation <span class="diag-head-long">around a product</span></span><span id="diag-q-label">Question 01</span></div>
      {# A Bauhaus orrery, built by field.js: the product at the centre,
         participant groups on offset elliptical orbits, a faint outer orbit
         for groups specific to the product. Each question sets a distinct
         state of the same system. The viewBox holds every state with
         clearance; nothing meaningful is clipped. #}
      <svg class="orrery-svg" id="orrery-field" viewBox="-60 16 800 568" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" role="img" aria-label="Orrery instrument: your product at the centre, with users, developers, creators, partners and advocates on offset orbits and a faint outer orbit for other participant groups. Selecting a question changes the state of the instrument."></svg>
      <div class="q-explain" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="q-card" data-q="0"><span class="q-src">Reading · from About</span><p>We begin with the people around a product and the relationships between them, not with the assumption that the answer is another Discord, forum, or community platform.</p></div>
        <div class="q-card" data-q="1"><span class="q-src">Participation design</span><p>Start with what participants are trying to accomplish, what they contribute and what would make involvement worthwhile for them.</p></div>
        <div class="q-card" data-q="2"><span class="q-src">Reading · Field Note, Aug 2026</span><p>Instead of asking which channels need to be served next, the focus shifts to the interplay between different stakeholders around a company.</p></div>
        <div class="q-card" data-q="3"><span class="q-src">Responsibilities</span><p>Identify who can act on a contribution, across company teams and independent participants, and what support they need.</p></div>
        <div class="q-card" data-q="4"><span class="q-src">Follow-through</span><p>Decide who owns the next action and how the participant hears what changed. Useful knowledge needs a route into product, customer and partnership decisions.</p></div>
        <div class="q-card" data-q="5"><span class="q-src">Barriers and support</span><p>Find what people want to do but cannot do easily today, then test whether changes to access, support or coordination help.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# --------------------------------------------- SELECTED WORK: VIGNETTES #}
<section class="cases chapter" id="cases" data-chapter="05" data-title="Selected work">
  {# ENGAGEMENT MANIFEST (approved): the six selected engagements as one indexed instrument rail. The logos are
     selectable coordinates (tabs); one shared record below shows the active engagement's description and sector with
     its index. No autoplay: hover previews on pointer devices, click or keyboard selects, arrow keys move along the
     rail. All six records stay in the document; without JavaScript they stack as a compact list. Logos are optically
     normalised per mark (--lh), never stretched; company names live only in the accessible names. #}
  <div class="exp-grid">
    <div class="exp-head">
      <p class="kicker"><span class="node-dot node-dot-ochre"></span>Selected work</p>
      <h2 class="cases-h2">A decade of building community, developer and advocacy programs.</h2>
      <p class="cases-lead">Selected engagements across SaaS and AI, the public sector and gaming, shown with what was actually done.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="manifest" id="manifest" style="--engagement-count:{{ clients.selectedWork.length }}">
      <div class="mani-index" role="tablist" aria-label="Selected engagements">
        {% for client in clients.selectedWork %}
        <button type="button" role="tab" class="mani-logo" id="mani-tab-{{ loop.index }}" aria-selected="{% if loop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}" aria-controls="mani-rec-{{ loop.index }}" tabindex="{% if loop.first %}0{% else %}-1{% endif %}" aria-label="{{ client.name }}" data-logo="{{ client.name | lower | replace(' ', '-') }}" style="--logo-url:url('{{ client.logoPath }}');"><span class="mani-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        {% endfor %}
        <span class="mani-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>
      <ol class="mani-records" id="mani-records">
        {% for client in clients.selectedWork %}
        <li class="mani-rec{% if loop.first %} on{% endif %}" id="mani-rec-{{ loop.index }}" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="mani-tab-{{ loop.index }}">
          <span class="mani-no"><b>0{{ loop.index }}</b> / 0{{ clients.selectedWork.length }}</span>
          <p class="mani-proof">{{ client.proof }}</p>
          <span class="mani-tag">{{ client.tag }}</span>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------- PUBLIC THINKING: PREVIEW #}
<section class="pt pt-cel chapter" id="thinking" data-chapter="06" data-title="Public Thinking">
  {# THE CELESTIAL RESEARCHER (production): a presence built only from
     constellations holds an open field journal and writes into it. Background
     star field behind the whole section, the scene in the left 59%, the
     findings in the right column. Geometry: researcher.js. Decorative SVGs are
     aria-hidden; all editorial content is HTML text. Not animated yet. #}
  <svg class="cel-bg" data-researcher='{"part":"bg"}' aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"></svg>
  {# data-journal: the two latest observations, derived from the same piece list as the ledger (src/_data/journalPages.js) #}
  <div class="pt-field" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="cel-fig" id="researcher-scene" data-researcher='{"part":"scene","animate":true}' data-journal="{{ journalPages | dump | escape }}" focusable="false"></svg></div>
  <div class="pt-edit">
  <div class="pt-head">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker"><span class="node-dot node-dot-ochre"></span>Public Thinking</p>
      <h2 class="pt-h2">Live findings,<br>not a static portfolio.</h2>
      <p class="pt-sub">Research findings, executive one-pagers, case studies and field notes, tagged by format and by how much evidence currently supports them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="pt-body" id="pt-body">
    <svg class="pt-signal" id="pt-signal" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"></svg>
  <ol class="ledger" id="ledger">
    {% for piece in publicThinking %}
    <li class="ledger-row">
      <span class="ledger-date">{{ piece.date | readableDate }}</span>
      <span class="ledger-meta"><span class="entry-format">{{ piece.format }}</span><span class="entry-conf">{{ piece.confidence }}</span></span>
      <div class="ledger-main">
        <h3 class="ledger-title"><a href="{{ piece.url }}">{{ piece.title }}</a></h3>
        {% if piece.deck %}<p class="ledger-deck">{{ piece.deck }}</p>{% endif %}
        <span class="entry-topics">{% for t in piece.topics %}<span>{{ t }}</span>{% endfor %}</span>
      </div>
      <a class="entry-link ledger-link" href="{{ piece.url }}">Read {{ piece.format | lower }} →</a>
      {# the finding's own constellation: one identified object inside the larger field, crossing the record's edge #}
      {% if piece.motif %}<div class="rec-motif" aria-hidden="true">{{ ptConstellation(piece.motif, 'record', 'dark') }}</div>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  <div class="pt-foot">
    <aside class="research-launch" aria-labelledby="research-launch-title">
      <div class="research-launch-copy">
        <p class="research-launch-label"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Research in progress</p>
        <h3 id="research-launch-title">When Participant Knowledge<br>Enters AI Answers</h3>
        <p class="research-launch-deck">{{ researchTeaser.en }}</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="research-rocket" viewBox="0 0 320 360" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <g transform="rotate(35 160 150)">
          <g class="rocket-lines">
            <path d="M150 28L169 65L179 110L178 168L162 210L138 210L122 168L121 110L131 65Z M131 65L169 65 M122 168L138 210 M178 168L162 210 M121 142L96 192L94 226L133 200 M179 142L204 192L206 226L167 200 M138 210L140 229L150 244L160 229L162 210"/>
            <path d="M150 91L163 97L169 111L163 125L150 131L137 125L131 111L137 97Z"/>
          </g>
